AXRB licensing map
==================

This repository contains separately licensed components. It is not licensed
in its entirety under MIT or under the AXRB Source-Available License.

1. New AXRB-owned contributions in licenses/source-available-files.txt,
   introduced after baseline commit
   19653e2c29e9cd93c25f8d0c906fa54e4c05b3c3, are offered under the AXRB
   Source-Available License 1.0 in licenses/AXRB-Source-Available-1.0.txt.
   Only contributions whose relevant rights the Licensor controls are covered.
   Listing a file does not assert ownership of its pre-existing contents.

2. The launcher is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later; see launcher/LICENSE
   and launcher/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The source-available restrictions do
   not apply to the launcher, its modifications, or other GPL-covered work.
   Previously MIT-licensed launcher portions retain their separate grant.

3. Previously released MIT code retains the permissions granted with those
   copies. The original MIT notice is preserved in licenses/MIT-legacy.txt.
   This change does not revoke or narrow any earlier license grant.

4. Third-party code, imported experiments, generated third-party material and
   dependencies retain their respective licenses and notices. Those notices
   take precedence over the coverage list. See launcher/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
   and the individual source files. This license grants no third-party rights.

5. Unlisted AXRB-owned files retain the previous MIT terms unless they carry
   another explicit license. New files are not automatically source-available:
   they must be deliberately added to the coverage list after a rights check.

Restrictions apply to covered code, not merely to the AXRB name: renaming a
derivative does not remove them. Independent programs, including the GPL
launcher, retain their own rights even when distributed alongside AXRB.

Read CONTRIBUTING.md before submitting changes. Request separate permissions
from the maintainers at https://github.com/Android-XR-Bridge/AXRB.
